    {
      "id": "396",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 396,
        "relationship_type": "antonym",
        "body": "やすい and にくい express opposite ideas: 'easy to do' and 'hard to do.' Both attach to verb stems, e.g. 食べやすい 'easy to eat' and 食べにくい 'hard to eat', and function as い-adjectives, meaning they can be seen with tenses like 食べやすかった 'was easy to eat', and modify nouns like with 食べやすい果物 'an easy-to-eat fruit'.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 90,
          "slug": "やすい",
          "title": "やすい",
          "meaning": "Easy to, Likely to",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 100,
          "slug": "にくい",
          "title": "にくい",
          "meaning": "Difficult to, Hard to",
          "level": "JLPT4",
